  <body>
    <sec id="s1">
      <title>Introduction</title>
      <p id="p1">High blood pressure is a leading cause of cardiovascular disease <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r1">1</xref>. Earlier trials of related agents were small <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r2">2</xref>,<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r3">3</xref>.</p>
    </sec>
    <sec id="s2">
      <title>Methods</title>
      <sec id="s2-1">
        <title>Design and participants</title>
        <p id="p2">This was a multicentre, double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled trial. Adults aged 18 years or older with hypertension were eligible. Exclusion criteria included pregnancy and severe renal disease. A total of 238 patients were randomly assigned in a 1:1 ratio to receive Drug A 10 mg once daily (n = 120) or placebo (n = 118). Patients were followed for 12 months.</p>
      </sec>
      <sec id="s2-2">
        <title>Outcomes and statistical analysis</title>
        <p id="p3">The primary outcome was major cardiovascular events at 12 months. Secondary outcomes included all-cause death and change in systolic blood pressure. Analyses followed the intention-to-treat principle. The model is given in <xref ref-type="disp-formula" rid="e1">equation 1</xref>.</p>
        <disp-formula id="e1">
          <label>(1)</label>
          <tex-math><![CDATA[y = \beta_0 + \beta_1 x + \varepsilon]]></tex-math>
          <mml:math><mml:mi>y</mml:mi><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mi>&#x3b2;</mml:mi><mml:mn>0</mml:mn></mml:msub><mml:mo>+</mml:mo><mml:msub><mml:mi>&#x3b2;</mml:mi><mml:mn>1</mml:mn></mml:msub><mml:mi>x</mml:mi><mml:mo>+</mml:mo><mml:mi>&#x3b5;</mml:mi></mml:math>
        </disp-formula>
      </sec>
    </sec>
    <sec id="s3">
      <title>Results</title>
      <p id="p4">Of the 238 randomized patients, 230 were included in the analysis. The primary outcome occurred in 24 of 120 patients (20.0%) in the Drug A group and 36 of 118 patients (30.5%) in the placebo group (hazard ratio 0.62, 95% CI 0.41 to 0.94; P = 0.02). Baseline characteristics are shown in <xref ref-type="table" rid="t1">Table 1</xref> and outcomes in <xref ref-type="table" rid="t2">Table 2</xref>.</p>
      <table-wrap id="t1">
